note How a file becomes symbols and calls when no language server answers for it. parse_file runs the language's tree-sitter grammar once over the text; a walk of the syntax tree picks out top-level declarations plus one level into impl/mod/trait/class bodies, notes what each import statement brings into scope, and records every call site as a bare (name, qualifier) pair. Nothing is resolved here: the call sites are strings, and link turns them into edges afterwards (see call-resolution). This backend runs for every file that is not cached, and is the final answer for a language whose server is missing or does not exist. Syntax colouring happens in the same parse; that half is the highlighting path.

